---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';

const description =
  'How ScrubKit handles your data: everything runs in your browser, nothing is uploaded, there are no accounts, cookies or trackers.';
---

<Base title="Privacy — Nothing You Paste Leaves Your Browser | ScrubKit" description={description}>
  <div class="container-page pt-8">
    <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy' }]} />

    <header class="mt-6 max-w-3xl">
      <span class="eyebrow text-ink-3">Privacy</span>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-extrabold sm:text-5xl">
        Nothing you paste leaves your browser.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg text-ink-2">
        This page is the boring, specific version of that promise.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-page mt-10 max-w-3xl">
      <h2>What happens to your text</h2>
      <p>
        ScrubKit is a static website: HTML, CSS and JavaScript files served from
        a CDN. When you paste text into a tool, the transformation runs as
        JavaScript inside your browser tab. There is no upload request, no API
        call and no server-side processing — the code that cleans your text is
        the same code that draws the page.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you close the tab, whatever you pasted is gone. We do not keep a
        copy because no copy was ever made outside your device.
      </p>

      <h2>What we store</h2>
      <p>
        Tool <strong>options</strong> (for example “case-sensitive comparison”
        or your preferred slug separator) are saved in your browser's
        localStorage so the tool behaves the way you left it on your next visit.
        That preference storage lives on your device and can be cleared at any
        time from your browser settings. <strong>Your pasted text is never
        written to localStorage</strong>, cookies, IndexedDB or anywhere else.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        There are no cookies. There are no analytics scripts, no session
        recorders, no advertising networks and no third-party requests on tool
        pages. If you open your browser's network panel while using a tool,
        you'll see the page load and nothing else.
      </p>

      <h2>Accounts</h2>
      <p>
        There are none. No signup, no login, no email collection, no password
        database — because there is no backend to hold one.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
      <p>
        The site's files are served by our static host, which keeps standard
        technical access logs (IP address, user agent, requested path, time)
        for security and abuse prevention, as almost every web host does. Those
        logs contain the URLs requested — never the content of your pasted
        text, which is never transmitted in the first place.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If any part of this ever changes — for example, if a future feature
        genuinely needs a server — it will be stated here in plain language
        before that feature exists, and it will be opt-in. The core promise
        (“nothing you paste is uploaded”) is the product; it is not for sale.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
